<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27306" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxo</span></b> , āvi, ātum, 1,
			v. a.
		Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοξός</span>, slanting, akin to
			obliquus, limus, licinus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to put out of joint, to dislocate</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxatum si quod est, sanum faciet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 157</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxata in locum reponere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 104, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">articulis luxatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 9, 23, § 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxata corpora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 6, 37, § 71</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to put out of
				place, displace</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxare vitium radices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 24, 37, § 227</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxatae machinae,</span>”
				<i>fallen apart</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					36, 15, 24, § 119</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luxata cornua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					45, 70, § 179</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
